uuid "1b651561-8f3c-5dbc-aa84-6fde737a1f47" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320129 1145 "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nSince we know the first two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${a}_{1}=-3,$ $d=3,$ and ${S}_{N}=27$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 27 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2(-3)+(N-1)(3)) \\\\ 54 & =N(-6+3N-3) \\\\ 54 & =N(3N-9) \\\\ 54 & =3{N}^{2}-9N\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the above equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{N}^{2}-9N-54 & =0 \\\\ {N}^{2}-3N-18 & =0 \\\\ (N-6)(N+3) & =0 \\\\ N & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive solution because $N$ can't be negative." 13194139534922 true] [17592186320130 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320131 13194139534922 true] [17592186320130 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320132 13194139534922 true] [17592186320130 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320133 13194139534922 true] [17592186320130 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320134 13194139534922 true] [17592186320130 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320135 13194139534922 true] [17592186320130 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534922 true] [17592186320130 1041 "selection" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320130 1104 #edb/ref 17592186320135 13194139534922 true] [17592186320130 1110 #uuid "32fba71b-d306-58c0-8593-e4f7022c16a5" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320131 1034 "9" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320131 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534922 true] [17592186320131 1111 #uuid "5cfeeb64-956b-5a03-b3f1-9652d75af5dc" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320132 1034 "3" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320132 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534922 true] [17592186320132 1111 #uuid "9026bb4f-91e3-5fc2-81df-e0daa5756744" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320133 1034 "15" 13194139534922 true] 