ic series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nSince we know the first two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =36-12 \\\\  & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${a}_{1}=12$, $d=24$, and ${S}_{N}=588$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 588 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2(12)+(N-1)(24)) \\\\ 588 & =\\frac{N}{2}(24+24N-24) \\\\ 588 & =\\frac{N}{2}(24N) \\\\ 588 & =12{N}^{2} \\\\ 49 & ={N}^{2} \\\\ N & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because $N$ can't be negative." 13194139534922 true] [17592186320172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320173 13194139534922 true] [17592186320172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320174 13194139534922 true] [17592186320172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320175 13194139534922 true] [17592186320172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320176 13194139534922 true] [17592186320172 1000 #edb/ref 17592186320177 13194139534922 true] [17592186320172 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534922 true] [17592186320172 1041 "selection" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320172 1104 #edb/ref 17592186320176 13194139534922 true] [17592186320172 1110 #uuid "27903b18-02c3-50a1-b22d-f43d11e66a94" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320173 1034 "9" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320173 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534922 true] [17592186320173 1111 #uuid "ff20f1da-c379-526b-b3ae-84ac11f270fa" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320174 1034 "11" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534922 true] [17592186320174 1111 #uuid "cab9cadb-055b-5a1f-bee2-16324732410f" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320175 1034 "8" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534922 true] [17592186320175 1111 #uuid "e496d045-25ea-5cc7-adc4-4855e271b577" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320176 1034 "7" 13194139534922 true] [17592186320176 1103 #edb/